    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451-a1">

                <pb facs="0807" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 130.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lynch to Mr.
                            Turner.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 28, 1874</date>.
                        (Received June 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The people of this city, desirous of having
                    themselves recorded among the mourners over the death of the late Hon. Charles
                    Sumner, of your country, at two well-attended town-meetings, on the 7th and 13th
                    of May, passed certain resolutions, a copy of which, and a copy of the minutes,
                    I have the honor herewith to forward to you. They will better explain the object
                    of this note.</p>
                <p>I am, Mr. Minister, very truly, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. H. LYNCH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
